    "evidence_text": "The PolyResponse engine is trained on hundreds of millions of examples extracted from real conversations: it learns what responses are appropriate in different conversational contexts.\n\nWe introduce a restaurant search and booking system powered by the PolyResponse engine, currently available in 8 different languages.\n\npaper, we present a demo system based on an alternative approach to task-oriented dialogue.\n\nRelying on non-generative response retrieval we describe the PolyResponse conversational search engine and its application in the task of restaurant search and booking.\n\nDue to its retrieval-based design, with the PolyResponse engine there is no need to engineer a structured ontology, or to solve\n\nthe difficult task of general language generation.\n\nThis design also bypasses the construction of dedicated decision-making policy modules.\n\nIn simple words, it is a ranking model that\n\nlearns to score conversational replies and images in a given conversational context.\n\nThe highest-scoring responses are then retrieved as system outputs.\n\nWe provide only a brief recap here; see the original paper for further details.\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: Text Representation.\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: Photo Representation.\n\nThis provides\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: Data Source 1: Reddit.\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: Data Source 2: Yelp.\n\nOnce the text encoding\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: Index of Responses.\n\nPolyResponse: Conversational Search ::: PolyResponse in a Nutshell.\n\n$t$ is a CNN pretrained on ImageNet, with a shallow one-layer DNN on top.\n\n$c$ , and finding nearby $h_r$ and $h_p$ vectors.\n\nThe system offers both voice and text input and output.\n\nSpeech-to-text and text-to-speech conversion in the PolyResponse system is currently supported by the off-the-shelf Google Cloud tools.\n\nThis flow is summarised here:  S1.\n\nGiven the\n\ndisplayed.\n\nThese classifiers are briefly discussed in \u00a7SECREF4.\n\nOther Functionality ::: Multilinguality.",
